// Signing for the three §11 spike targets — one place, not three.
//
// DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is the 10-character Team ID of the sandbox team: the personal free team
// or the studio paid login (§4.3). It is a *signing* identity, so the throwaway rule applies
// to the bundle IDs it signs — never a production identifier, never an App Store Connect
// record. The spike apps never ship.
//
// Find it in Xcode → Settings → Accounts → your Apple ID → the team row (right-hand column),
// or in any target's Signing & Capabilities editor once a team is selected.
//
// Free-team mechanics, for when this starts biting: 10 App IDs, 3 devices per platform,
// 3 installed dev apps per device, and profiles that expire after 7 days — rebuild the
// morning of any demo (§4.3, pitfall 12).

// Left blank deliberately: each contributor signs with their own team.
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// T14 — build once WITHOUT the background-delivery entitlement, deliberately, and verify the
// arming failure surfaces as BG_DELIVERY_FAILED with the engine in armFailed while foreground
// catch-up keeps working (§14 T14). CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS is set per target in the project,
// so drive T14 from the command line rather than from here:
//
//   xcodebuild ... CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS=Entitlements/BPSpikeQ-NoBackgroundDelivery.entitlements
